WHERE IT COMES FROM

PicoQuorum, by Jason McPheron (MIT): a hardware console that is one owner of a Safe. Sign and Burn
  began in its repository. console/safe_tx.py, console/decode.py and console/webauthn.py come from
  its console, site/src/blockies.mjs and site/src/webauthn.mjs from its pages, tools/fingerprint.mjs
  from its release tools, and console/test/safe_tx.json and passkey.json from its test vectors.

picowallet, by Austin Griffith (https://github.com/austintgriffith/picowallet), MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Austin Griffith. PicoQuorum began as a fork of it. console/keccak.py comes from
  it and says so on its first line. It is under the MIT license in LICENSE, which carries Austin
  Griffith's copyright.

MicroPython (https://micropython.org), MIT, Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Damien P. George and others:
  the WebAssembly build the page runs the console on, in docs/vendor/micropython/ with its notice.

viem, @noble/hashes, @noble/curves, @scure/base, abitype and ox, MIT: bundled into docs/app.js, with
  their notices at the end of that file.

Blockies (https://github.com/ethereum/blockies): site/src/blockies.mjs draws the same identicons,
  ported from its algorithm.

console/cfg.py holds the SafeWebAuthnSignerProxy's creation code (safe-modules passkey 0.2.1,
  LGPL-3.0, Safe Ecosystem Foundation), so the console can work out a passkey's signer address. It is
  in the built site too, in docs/console/cfg.py.

tools/chain/code.json holds the runtime bytecode of contracts deployed on Base Sepolia, fetched from
  the chain, for the tests and the local chain only:
    Safe 1.4.1 (SafeL2, SafeProxyFactory, CompatibilityFallbackHandler, MultiSendCallOnly), LGPL-3.0,
      Safe Ecosystem Foundation (https://github.com/safe-global/safe-smart-account)
    SafeWebAuthnSignerFactory and SafeWebAuthnSignerSingleton (safe-modules passkey 0.2.1), LGPL-3.0,
      Safe Ecosystem Foundation (https://github.com/safe-global/safe-modules)
    Daimo's P-256 verifier, MIT (https://github.com/daimo-eth/p256-verifier)
    Multicall3, MIT (https://github.com/mds1/multicall)
    The deterministic deployment proxy, Unlicense, Arachnid (https://github.com/Arachnid/deterministic-deployment-proxy)
